# .gitignore for a Go project
# Ignore common build artifacts, OS/editor files, and secrets

# Binaries and build output
/bin/
/build/
/out/
/dist/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
envisible

# Test outputs
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
*.coverprofile

# Vendor dependencies (uncomment if you vendor dependencies)
# vendor/

# Generated object files
*.o
*.a
*.lo

# Logs and temporary files
*.log
*.tmp
*_tmp

# Editor and IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.swp
*.swo
*.class

# macOS & Windows system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment / secret files
*.env
*.env.local
*.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.crt
*.cert
secrets.*

# Misc
# Ignore compiled Go packages (cache is not usually in repo, but keep this for safety)
*.test

# Notes:
# - Keep `go.sum` and source directories such as `pkg/` and `cmd/` tracked.
# - If you already committed secrets (e.g. bad.env), remove them from Git tracking:
#     git rm --cached bad.env && git commit -m "stop tracking bad.env"
